          "subComponents": [
            {
              "title": "Cybersecurity Operations Planner",
              "caption": "Jul 2020 - May 2023 · 2 yrs 10 mos",
              "metadata": "United States",
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Assigned to gain experience at the strategic level of command, guaranteeing the nation’s security and the security of allies in collaboration with over 4K personnel positioned across the globe. Work within the Joint Cyber Center to plan offensive and defensive cyber operations across the globe in support of strategic deterrence. Interface with DoD stakeholders at the Combatant Command level to plan, coordinate, and track offensive and defensive cyber operations, specifically working with US Cyber Command, US North Command, US Europe Command, and US Space Command.\n\n✔  Spearheaded a team of 300+ members distributed across the globe, conducted Tabletop Exercises to familiarize and test effectiveness of cyber hardening framework.\n\n✔ Created and implemented a first-of-its-kind and globally impactful defensive cyber hardening framework/construct based on the MITRE Attack framework for a DoD strategic deterrence enabling capability.\n\n✔ Gained recognition at the top levels of DoD for cyber hardening efforts which were briefed to Congress.\n\n✔  Elevated the awareness and importance of defending ICS/SCADA and achieved the highest level of readiness regarding the defensive posture of systems dating back to the Cold War Era due to framework effectiveness.\n\n✔  Demonstrated advanced leadership aptitude and leveraged experience as Squadron Commander to change the climate of the small office staff.\n\n✔  Onboarded military officers to examine the root problem of prior workplace failures and formed a new strategy to empower employees to find joy in daily jobs/missions, efforts which brought significant success in a short time."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Cyberspace Operations Officer",
              "caption": "2005 - May 2023 · 18 yrs 4 mos",
              "metadata": "United States",
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "As an Air Force cyberspace operations officer, I lead personnel in the defense of critical mission systems, networks, and infrastructure.  During this time, the Air Force Cyberspace community has transitioned from a culture of prioritizing availability to now prioritizing integrity and confidentiality.\n\n✔  Taken on roles of ever-increasing complexity and responsibility from management of small teams to the equivalent of a CIO/CISO of a medium sized company.\n\n✔  Honed my communication skills; I am adept at translating highly technical cybersecurity language to effectively communicate to executive leadership and stakeholders expressing the value of cybersecurity.\n \n✔  Adept at forming, growing, and leading teams of experts and recognize that giving them recognition and expressing that I value their talents and contributions are force multipliers.\n\n✔  Awarded the Company Grade Officer Information Dominance Award out of ~3.5K fellow officers which compares to middle management within the corporate world and recognizes exemplary efforts in the field of cyber defense."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Cyber Squadron Commander",
              "caption": "Jan 2018 - Jul 2020 · 2 yrs 6 mos",
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Supported one of only three Air Force Bases with F-15E Strike Eagles. Managed a limited $750K budget and 80+ personnel with the collective purpose of providing, maintaining, and defending mission systems and supporting communication infrastructure. Enhanced the partnership between strategic cyber defense direction from the Combatant Command level with the Wing Commander’s mission to protect and assure the F-15 Strike Eagle capability.  Advanced risk management, information security, and project/program management principles.\n\n✔  Highly competitive role; selected from a list of ~1.5K Air Force Cyber Officers to fill position due to proven ability to lead and solve problems at the operational and tactical level.\n\n✔  Carried out daily responsibilities similar to that of a CIO of a small to medium sized company.\n\n✔  Developed a culture of empowerment and innovation to achieve the best defensive cyber posture in the Air Force, efforts which were sustained for the second year of command and into the next command.\n\n✔  Established a specialized training plan to equip a small team of Airmen to deploy active sensing technology on critical mission systems to thwart the adversary’s attempts to infiltrate and increase mission resiliency.\n\n✔  Reorganized the workforce to address and enhance the squadron’s ability to defend critical systems and significantly revitalized a culture of low morale with no strategic direction and mediocre performance levels.\n\n✔  Advocated for additional funding for new technology to increase cyber defense and efficiency, resulting in approval to purchase initiatives which greatly enhanced the defensive posture."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Resource Manager",
              "caption": "Jan 2016 - Dec 2017 · 1 yr 11 mos",
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Deployed to directly support the Army Major General in charge of the forward command center. Served as a project planner and collected IT requirements prior to packaging them and advocating for purchase. Selected for position based upon project management experience combined with ability to translate complex IT jargon into comprehensive terminology for delivery to senior leaders.\n\n✔  Researched and briefed solutions and implementation planning to ensure Win 10 compliance, a significant investment which replaced every workstation in Afghanistan and was executed ahead of schedule with zero hindrances."
                }
